    "b-dw-cut-h": {
      "id": "b-dw-cut-h",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The app is a deliverable cut, not a library"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dw-cut-d": {
      "id": "b-dw-cut-d",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision: docs-workbench owns only deliverable-level concerns — server startup, browser routing, transport and session policy, host-provided embeds, settings persistence, and desktop lifecycle. The Bun host mounts docs-server's route factory rather than copying write rules; the React host composes docs-viewer surfaces rather than defining block rendering or editor semantics. No lower package imports it; docs-cli lazy-loads it for "
        },
        {
          "insert": "serve",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "export",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dw-cut-w": {
      "id": "b-dw-cut-w",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why: None of these concerns changes the document format, write authority, or viewer contract, so they stay replaceable glue — another host can embed either side without inheriting this shell, and the shell can change without moving the contracts below it. Rejected: a load-bearing app that reimplements either side."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dw-cut-a": {
      "id": "b-dw-cut-a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to: "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/docs-workbench",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — every future host feature stays composition glue."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dw-data-h": {
      "id": "b-dw-data-h",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Host policy lives in web/src/data"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dw-data-d": {
      "id": "b-dw-data-d",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision: Transport, hash, and session policy attach in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/docs-workbench/web/src/data",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/docs-workbench/web/src/data"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "api.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " selects live "
        },
        {
          "insert": "api/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " requests or exported "
        },
        {
          "insert": "data/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " files and owns HTTP and SSE policy, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "client.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " adapts that layer to the viewer's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "DocsClient",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " seam, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "session.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " defines the one per-tab actor id shared by locks, writes, and event filtering. Viewer components never learn URLs or response envelopes."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dw-data-w": {
      "id": "b-dw-data-w",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why: One transport boundary and one actor identity keep lock ownership, writes, and self-echo filtering naming the same session; scattering fetch calls through pages was rejected because policy then diverges per surface."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-dw-data-a": {
      "id": "b-dw-data-a",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
